    <section class="section" id="extras" aria-labelledby="extras-title"><div class="shell"><div class="section-intro reveal"><div><div class="section-kicker">Optional extras</div><h2 id="extras-title">Add the finishing touches your clean needs.</h2></div><p>Extras are priced separately from the core clean, so you only add the tasks your home needs.</p></div><div class="pricing-extras-grid">${pricingExtraCardsMarkup}</div><p class="booking-policy-note booking-policy-note--extras"><strong>Extras are one-off.</strong> They apply to your first service only, are not repeated on recurring visits and are not eligible for frequency discounts.</p><div class="lease-included reveal"><span class="lease-included__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"><path d="M12 22s8-3.7 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6.3 8 10 8 10Z"></path><path d="m8.5 12 2.2 2.2 4.8-5"></path></svg></span><p><strong>Booking End of Lease or Move In?</strong> Inside oven, inside kitchen cabinets and inside all other cabinets are already included. Do not add them again as extras.</p></div></div></section>

    <section class="section section--soft" id="price-factors" aria-labelledby="factors-title"><div class="shell"><div class="section-intro reveal"><div><div class="section-kicker">What shapes the price</div><h2 id="factors-title">Four choices shape the price.</h2></div><p>The calculator changes only when one of these practical parts of the booking changes.</p></div><div class="factors-grid reveal"><article class="factor"><span class="factor__num">01</span><h3>Service type</h3><p>Standard, Deep, Move In, End of Lease and Hourly each have a different scope and starting rate.</p></article><article class="factor"><span class="factor__num">02</span><h3>Bedrooms or hours</h3><p>Flat rates scale with the number of bedrooms. Hourly cleaning scales with booked team time.</p></article><article class="factor"><span class="factor__num">03</span><h3>Frequency</h3><p>Get 10% off weekly and fortnightly bookings, or 5% off 3-weekly and monthly bookings, from your second service.</p></article><article class="factor"><span class="factor__num">04</span><h3>Extras</h3><p>Flat-rate services add optional tasks separately; Hourly selections use booked time and are not charged as extras.</p></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="payment-section" id="payment" aria-labelledby="payment-title"><div class="shell payment-panel"><div class="payment-cell"><div class="section-kicker">Payment, without the awkward part</div><h2 id="payment-title">Securely held. Charged after the clean.</h2></div><div class="payment-cell"><span class="payment-cell__label">Before the service</span><h3>Your card secures the booking.</h3><p>A temporary hold is generally placed two days before the service, or immediately for short-notice bookings.</p></div><div class="payment-cell"><span class="payment-cell__label">After the service</span><h3>The final amount is charged.</h3><p>Payment is processed after the clean, once the service details and any approved changes are confirmed.</p></div></div></section>

    <section class="section faq-section" id="faqs" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="faq-layout shell"><div class="faq-intro reveal"><div class="section-kicker">Pricing questions</div><h2 id="faq-title">House cleaning price FAQs.</h2><p>Clear answers about estimates, discounts, hours and payment. For worked examples, read our <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-melbourne/">2026 Melbourne cleaning cost guide</a>.</p><a class="text-link" href="mailto:info@maidathome.com.au">Ask our team <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"><path d="M4 10h11M11 6l4 4-4 4"></path></svg></a></div><div class="faq-list reveal"><article class="faq-item is-open"><h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="priceFaq1" id="priceQuestion1">Are the calculator prices final?<span class="faq-question__icon"></span></button></h3><div class="faq-answer" id="priceFaq1" role="region" aria-labelledby="priceQuestion1"><div><p>The calculator provides an instant estimate based on the choices entered. We confirm service details and availability before assigning the booking, and any approved changes are reflected in the final amount.</p></div></div></article><article class="faq-item"><h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="priceFaq2" id="priceQuestion2">Why is there a two-hour minimum for Hourly Cleaning?<span class="faq-question__icon"></span></button></h3><div class="faq-answer" id="priceFaq2" role="region" aria-labelledby="priceQuestion2"><div><p>Two hours provides enough booked team time to complete meaningful work after arrival, setup and understanding your priorities.</p></div></div></article><article class="faq-item"><h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="priceFaq3" id="priceQuestion3">When does my recurring discount begin?<span class="faq-question__icon"></span></button></h3><div class="faq-answer" id="priceFaq3" role="region" aria-labelledby="priceQuestion3"><div><p>Your first service is charged at the normal one-off rate. The eligible 10% or 5% discount applies from the second recurring service.</p></div></div></article><article class="faq-item"><h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="priceFaq4" id="priceQuestion4">How are team hours counted?<span class="faq-question__icon"></span></button></h3><div class="faq-answer" id="priceFaq4" role="region" aria-labelledby="priceQuestion4"><div><p>Booked time is total team time. Two cleaners working for one hour use two cleaning hours; one cleaner working for two hours also uses two cleaning hours.</p></div></div></article><article class="faq-item"><h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="priceFaq5" id="priceQuestion5">Are oven and cabinet interiors extra for End of Lease?<span class="faq-question__icon"></span></button></h3><div class="faq-answer" id="priceFaq5" role="region" aria-labelledby="priceQuestion5"><div><p>No. Inside oven, inside kitchen cabinets and inside all other cabinets are included in the End of Lease core service, so the calculator disables those extras when End of Lease is selected.</p></div></div></article><article class="faq-item"><h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="priceFaq6" id="priceQuestion6">When is my card charged?<span class="faq-question__icon"></span></button></h3><div class="faq-answer" id="priceFaq6" role="region" aria-labelledby="priceQuestion6"><div><p>A temporary hold generally secures the booking before the service. The final amount is processed after the clean once the confirmed details are known.</p></div></div></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="final-title"><div class="final-cta__panel">__ASTRO_IMAGE_1__<div class="final-cta__inner shell"><div class="final-cta__content reveal"><span class="final-cta__eyebrow">A clear price starts here</span><h2 id="final-title">Build the clean that fits your home.</h2><p>Choose service, size or hours, frequency and extras. See the estimate before you continue.</p><a class="button button--primary" href="#price-calculator">Calculate my price <span class="button__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"><path d="M4 10h11M11 6l4 4-4 4"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></div></section>
  </main>`);
const contentParts = content.split(/__ASTRO_IMAGE_\d+__/);
const images: Array<Record<string, any>> = [
  {
    src: "/assets/generated/pricing/pricing-hero.png",
    alt: "Bright comfortable home ready to enjoy after cleaning",
    width: 1000,
    height: 667,
    fetchpriority: "high",
  },
  {
    src: "/assets/generated/pricing/pricing-cta.png",
    alt: "Peaceful sunlit home after professional cleaning",
    width: 2200,
    height: 1467,
    loading: "lazy",
    class: "final-cta__image",
  },
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  styles={styles}
  scripts={scripts}
  preHeader={preHeader}
  legacyHeader={false}
  skipLink={true}
  yearId="year"
  currentPath="/pricing"
  bodyClass=""
>
  {
    contentParts.map((part, index) => (
      <>
        <Fragment set:html={part} />
        {images[index] && <OptimizedImage {...images[index]} />}
      </>
    ))
  }
</SiteLayout>
